        "description": "RTX 5090: upstream's own lossless 5090 config -- FlashAttention2 plus text-encoder CPU offload.",
        "notes": "Transcribed from configs/qwen_image_21/qwen_image_21_5090.json -- the NON-quantized 5090 config, which upstream ships alongside the FP8 ones. FA2 against sglang's Torch SDPA is a fair swap: both are exact softmax, and this repo's rule is that each framework gets its fastest kernel of the same precision class. MEASURED 2026-09-21 on a 1x RTX 5090 devbox, LightX2V main 4d709c43 inside upstream's own image (lightx2v/lightx2v:26062001-cu130-5090-fix-260921, torch 2.11.0+cu130, base.sh confirming BF16 with no sensitive-layer override): p50 14.51s, and unlike the H200 it is perfectly unimodal (seven repeats all 14.51) because its compute sits safely below the 14.5s tick boundary and pays a flat ~0.36s. Interleaved ABAB against sglang on the SAME node, 3 rounds x 5 requests: sglang 14.087 / 14.096 / 14.080 against LightX2V 14.514 / 14.513 / 14.512 -- paired diffs +2.9%, +2.9%, +3.0%, 3/3 agreeing in sign, round-to-round spread 0.1% on both sides. This one resolves (the H200 pair does not). About a third of that is the tick; server-side the gap is ~1.9% (sglang 13.879s vs 14.10-14.20s). The memory difference is the one that is not marginal: 17.0 GB steady against 30.7 GB on a 32 GB card. Output equivalence was checked rather than assumed: both return a 1024x1024 PNG at color type 6 (RGBA), LightX2V's alpha carrying real data (range 253-255). The response-size difference is the envelope, not the image -- sglang's 2.43 MB is base64 JSON around a ~1.83 MB PNG against LightX2V's 1.88 MB of raw PNG -- so there is no encode-cost asymmetry between them. INSTALL: do NOT use scripts/install_comparison_frameworks.sh for this -- it builds flash-attn 2.8.3 from source, which cannot compile against torch 2.14+cu130 (flash-attn pins -std=c++17, torch's ATen needs C++20, and 2.8.3.post1 is the newest PyPI release). Upstream's image has flash_attn, flash_attn_interface, flashinfer and sageattention prebuilt. Note also that the tag in LightX2V's README (26062001) does not exist; real tags carry a platform suffix.",
